<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Intelligent Robots</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> How Technology Changes Society</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Develop instructions for everyday tasks. Interactive: Revise classmates' essays on general topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can develop step-by-step instructions for using AI tools in everyday life, using simple language for clarity (e.g., "Open the app and select a task to get suggestions from the AI assistant.") Can edit and revise essays on AI, ensuring clarity in descriptions of technology (e.g., "Explain how AI assists in daily tasks like organizing schedules.") Can provide feedback on classmates' writing about AI, suggesting examples to clarify abstract ideas (e.g., "Add examples of AI used in customer service.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 40%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 40%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students individually write down one simple instruction for using a common smart device or AI tool they know (e.g., "To play music with your smart speaker, say 'Hey AI, play pop music.'"). The teacher asks a few students to share their written instructions, focusing on clarity and conciseness. This activates prior knowledge and sets the stage for writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to write a clear, step-by-step instruction by demonstrating on the board. For example, "How to use an AI translator app: 1. Open the app. 2. Select your languages. 3. Speak clearly into the microphone. 4. Read or listen to the translation." The teacher emphasizes using imperative verbs and numbering steps. Pronunciation of /ɑː/ in "adopt" or "job" can be modeled during this, connecting to a simple AI task.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do good instructions use long sentences or short, clear steps?" (Expected answer: Short, clear steps.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Why is it important to number the steps?" (Expected answer: To show the correct order.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Intelligent Robots".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short blog post (narrative excerpt) from an online tech magazine titled "AI in Our Daily Lives: Benefits and Challenges." The text will describe how AI systems are programmed (passive voice) and predict future impacts (future simple, conditionals), using vocabulary such as 'artificial intelligence,' 'technology,' 'opportunities,' 'challenges,' 'job markets,' 'evolve,' 'revolutionize,' 'enhance.' It will also contain an embedded example of simple instructions for using an AI assistant to manage a schedule.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Identifying key information and linguistic features in written texts to inform productive writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the blog post silently.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the main idea of this article about AI?" (Expected answer: AI brings both improvements and problems to society.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> Students decide if statements about the text are True or False, focusing on details about AI's impact and how it works (e.g., "AI systems are programmed to make human decisions without data input." - False).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students identify and underline all sentences using conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice in the text.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Developing written instructions and descriptive paragraphs using conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice, along with target vocabulary (e.g., 'advance,' 'evolve,' 'opportunities,' 'challenges,' 'integrate,' 'systems'). Practice pronunciation of multisyllabic words like "innovative" /ˈɪn.ə.veɪ.tɪv/ and "technological" /ˌtek.nəˈlɒdʒ.ɪ.kəl/ during teacher feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Transformation:</b> Students are given sentences about AI and asked to rewrite them using the specified grammar.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Rewrite using Passive Voice: 'Programmers develop artificial intelligence systems quickly.' → 'Artificial intelligence systems <b>are developed</b> quickly by programmers.'"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Combine with a Conditional: 'AI advances. Job markets change significantly.' → '<b>If</b> AI <b>continues to advance</b>, job markets <b>might change</b> significantly.'"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Rewrite using Future Simple: 'AI creates new jobs.' → 'AI <b>will create</b> new employment opportunities.'"</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Guided Paragraph Writing:</b> Students work individually to complete a short paragraph about "Intelligent Robots" using provided sentence starters and a word bank (e.g., 'advance,' 'evolve,' 'opportunities,' 'challenges,' 'society,' 'technological'). The paragraph will include blanks for conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice constructions. Example sentence starter: "If intelligent robots ______ (continue to evolve), our society ______ (will experience) significant changes. New employment opportunities ______ (create) and our daily experiences ______ (enhance)."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Peer Sentence Check:</b> In pairs, students exchange their completed paragraphs from the previous activity. They check each other's work for correct grammar (conditionals, future simple, passive voice), appropriate vocabulary use, and clarity. They mark any sentences that need improvement and provide constructive feedback. Teacher circulates, monitoring and assisting.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Intelligent Robots".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Writing and Peer Revision. Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group chooses one of two writing tasks:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Option A (Instructions):</b> Write clear, step-by-step instructions (5-7 steps) for using an imaginary AI tool designed to help people in everyday life (e.g., an AI personal assistant for managing tasks, a robot for customer service interactions, an AI for enhancing learning). Instructions must use simple language, imperative verbs, and clearly numbered steps. Students should consider how their "Intelligent Robot" will enable better experiences or functional improvements.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Option B (Essay Paragraph):</b> Write a paragraph (8-10 sentences) discussing how "Intelligent Robots" will change society in a specific area (e.g., job markets, healthcare, education). The paragraph must include at least two conditional forms, two examples of the future simple, and two uses of the passive voice. Students should use vocabulary from the list (e.g., 'revolutionize,' 'opportunities,' 'challenges,' 'technological,' 'societal'). This task encourages discussing AI's societal role sensitively.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After drafting, groups exchange their written pieces with another group for peer revision. They provide written feedback based on clarity, grammar, vocabulary use, and suggestions for adding examples to clarify abstract ideas (as per learning outcome).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer assessment using a checklist/rubric, followed by teacher observation and collection of revised written products.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group submits their final revised written piece (either instructions or essay paragraph) along with the peer feedback form they used. The teacher collects these for review, checking for adherence to task requirements.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer & Teacher):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of instructions/ideas.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of target grammar (conditional forms, future simple, passive voice).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of recommended vocabulary (e.g., 'artificial intelligence,' 'society,' 'opportunities,' 'challenges,' 'evolve,' 'integrate').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Organization and logical flow of ideas/steps.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of specific examples where relevant (for essays) or clear, sequential steps (for instructions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and constructive feedback during peer revision.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following prompts individually:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of writing today's instructions/paragraph, and how did you overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one piece of feedback you received that improved your writing?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-8 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident do you feel now about writing clear instructions or a paragraph discussing technology's impact using conditionals, future simple, and passive voice?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In what situations outside of English class do you think writing clear instructions or well-structured paragraphs about technology might be useful?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b> The writing activities successfully engaged students with the target grammar and vocabulary while focusing on clarity and organization. The peer revision process was effective in developing interactive writing skills. Some groups needed more guidance in incorporating varied vocabulary and providing specific examples in their essays. Adjustments for next lesson (Mediation) will include a brief review of key vocabulary to ensure comprehensive understanding before mediation tasks, and perhaps scaffolding for explaining complex ideas in simpler terms.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will use their developed writing skills to summarize information about AI's impact and present their ideas, potentially integrating their instructions or essay paragraphs into a larger project or presentation for the 21st Century Skills Project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>